course: dictionary
lesson: 7803
title: Quartz: a hard mineral and a steady clock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quartz is a mineral, which means a natural solid material. It is found in many rocks. «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica, formed deep underground.» So quartz is one of the parts that make up granite, and you can often spot it as clear or white crystals.
explain: Quartz is very hard. In science lessons it scores 7 on the Mohs scale, which is hard enough to scratch glass, and most grains of sand are quartz. When you meet the word, ask what the sentence is about. Rocks and sand mean the mineral; a watch or clock means the other meaning.
explain: «A quartz crystal in a watch vibrates 32,768 times every second.» The tiny crystal beats at a steady rate, and that steady beat keeps the watch accurate. So a quartz watch is a battery watch that keeps good time. Swap the meaning into the sentence to check: a steady-beat crystal in a watch makes sense.
fact: Quartz is a hard, common mineral, often clear or white.
fact: Quartz can form beautiful crystals with flat faces and sharp edges.
fact: Most grains of sand are quartz.
fact: A quartz watch keeps accurate time because its tiny quartz crystal vibrates at a steady rate.
fact: Quartz is hard enough to scratch glass.
exercise: «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica.» What is quartz in this sentence? | A sort of cloud | *A hard mineral that forms crystals | A kind of clock | A sea animal
exercise: «A quartz crystal in a watch vibrates 32,768 times every second.» What job does the crystal do? | It holds the battery in place | It makes the watch look shiny | *It beats at a steady rate to keep the time accurate | It sounds an alarm
exercise: Mia says «rose quartz» must be a type of watch. Is she right? | Yes, because it is a battery | *No, it is a coloured type of quartz, and some coloured types are gems | No, it is a kind of cloud | Yes, all quartz is a watch
test: What is a quartz watch? | A watch that only works in sand | A watch that shows the weather | A watch made of solid granite | *A battery watch with a quartz crystal that keeps accurate time
test: Most grains of sand are which mineral? | *Quartz | Salt | Coal | Granite
exam: Which description best fits quartz as a rock word? | A word for a rock that floats | *A hard, common mineral, often clear or white, found in many rocks and sand | A soft metal used in jewellery | A kind of cloud that brings rain
